{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And the remnant of Jacob</b> — those who were unable [to remain], who joined with the people of Bethlehem [?], for their place will be distant, for they are still in exile." "<b>Like dew from HaShem</b> — the meaning is that they will trust in HaShem alone and not in the kings of the nations who are in their land, like dew which is not in human authority but only in the hand of HaShem. Or: Israel will teach the nations to call upon the name of HaShem and they will be among them, in the manner of 'I will be like dew to Israel' [Hosea 14:6], and 'every nation will not hope in a man.'"], :book :micah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {0 "בית הלחמין (lit. 'house of the meat-eaters') is textually uncertain; possibly a corruption or a specific group designation. Translated hyper-literally as 'people of Bethlehem [?]' reflects the difficulty."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Micah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=20&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:14:02.187504407Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}